<http://data.silknow.org/object/422bb8cb-ac99-3416-9b73-39b4bbc4687e/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "White ground with a barn-yard scene printed in blue;  in one corner a windmill, below, a house, barn, hay-mow, trees, cattle, hay-makers and a gypsy.  Made with a linen warp and cotton weft, and printed from an engraved copper-plate;  At the time this was made, the English did not know how to make a strong enough cotton thread to be used as a warp, and had imported up to this date all their cotton cloth from India.  Mate to 87.21."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/422bb8cb-ac99-3416-9b73-39b4bbc4687e> .

